Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Equilibrium propagation is a promising energy-based alternative to backpropagation for
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.04,0:00:09.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}training neural networks on brains or neuromorphic hardware,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.91,0:00:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but it classically demands two things physical substrates cannot easily deliver: perfectly
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.72,0:00:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}symmetric weights and infinitesimally small nudges.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.00,0:00:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This ICLR 2024 paper from the Friedrich Miescher Institute and the University of Basel,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.61,0:00:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}by Axel Laborieux and Friedemann Zenke,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.13,0:00:32.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}cleanly separates the two resulting sources of gradient bias and shows how to remove them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.93,0:00:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Finite-nudge bias is eliminated exactly with a Cauchy integral,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.99,0:00:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while weight-asymmetry bias is tamed by a new homeostatic loss that penalizes asymmetry
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.60,0:00:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}of the Jacobian rather than the weights.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.18,0:00:47.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The payoff: for the first time,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.18,0:00:52.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}equilibrium propagation trains asymmetric networks on ImageNet 32 by 32 with only a small
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.92,0:00:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gap to the ideal symmetric case.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.28,0:00:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Equilibrium propagation, or EP,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.68,0:01:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}is an appealing way to train neural networks directly on physical substrates like brains or analog chips,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.08,0:01:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}because it computes gradients using only the network's own relaxation dynamics.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.49,0:01:12.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But it comes with two strict requirements: the weights must be perfectly symmetric,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.89,0:01:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the nudge that pushes the network toward its target must be infinitesimally small.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.29,0:01:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Both are very hard to satisfy in real physical hardware.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.69,0:01:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And crucially,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.10,0:01:30.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}whether weight asymmetry actually harms learning had never been pinned down,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.50,0:01:34.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}because in practice its effect gets tangled up with the error introduced by using a finite nudge.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.20,0:01:37.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The reason this matters is energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.49,0:01:42.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Physical neural systems, whether biological brains or neuromorphic chips,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.41,0:01:47.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}could train networks at a tiny fraction of the energy cost of digital hardware.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.74,0:01:51.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But backpropagation, the workhorse of deep learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.25,0:01:56.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}needs a separate linear backward pass and the exact transpose of every weight matrix,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.98,0:02:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}neither of which physical substrates provide naturally.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.68,0:02:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}EP sidesteps this, yet its own symmetry assumption is nearly as demanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.67,0:02:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And there was a warning sign: the asymmetric version of EP had only ever worked on toy
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.47,0:02:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}tasks like MNIST and outright failed on CIFAR-10.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.77,0:02:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Nobody had explained why.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.76,0:02:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper makes four contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.59,0:02:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.43,0:02:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it analytically separates the two sources of bias in generalized EP: the finite nudge
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.26,0:02:32.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the asymmetry of the network's Jacobian.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.09,0:02:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second, it extends holomorphic EP to asymmetric, complex-differentiable systems,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.93,0:02:39.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the exact error can be recovered even without weight symmetry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.76,0:02:43.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, and most practically,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.60,0:02:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it introduces a new homeostatic loss that reduces the asymmetry of the Jacobian directly,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.43,0:02:51.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rather than forcing the weights themselves to be symmetric.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.26,0:02:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And fourth, it demonstrates that with this loss,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.10,0:02:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}EP finally scales all the way up to ImageNet at thirty-two by thirty-two resolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.23,0:03:00.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The method has two parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.80,0:03:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To kill the finite-nudge bias,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.69,0:03:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors build on holomorphic EP: they drive the network with an oscillating teaching
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.24,0:03:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}signal and use a Cauchy integral from complex analysis to recover the exact error vector,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.84,0:03:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}no matter how large the nudge and even when the Jacobian is asymmetric.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.31,0:03:23.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Better still, this can be estimated continuously over many oscillation cycles,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.23,0:03:26.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}removing the need for separate free and nudged phases.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.63,0:03:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To tackle the second bias,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.27,0:03:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they show it grows with the skew-symmetric part of the Jacobian,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.30,0:03:36.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and introduce a homeostatic loss that penalizes exactly that part,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.45,0:03:39.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}estimated efficiently with the Hutchinson trace trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.86,0:03:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The key insight is that this improves functional symmetry of the Jacobian without ever
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.27,0:03:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}forcing the weights to be symmetric.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.84,0:03:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The experiments span four datasets of increasing difficulty.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.11,0:03:56.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On Fashion MNIST,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.37,0:04:00.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}small multilayer networks are used to cleanly isolate and measure each source of bias.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.64,0:04:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Then a recurrent convolutional architecture with genuinely asymmetric feedback weights is trained on CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.91,0:04:09.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CIFAR-100, and finally ImageNet at thirty-two by thirty-two,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.17,0:04:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which is where the homeostatic loss really earns its keep.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.44,0:04:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors also confirm in the appendix that the same loss helps predictive coding networks,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.70,0:04:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which have no reciprocal connections at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.27,0:04:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline result is striking.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.82,0:04:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.36,0:04:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the asymmetric network trained with EP but without the homeostatic loss reaches only sixty
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.91,0:04:36.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}point four percent accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.45,0:04:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Add the homeostatic loss, and accuracy jumps to eighty-four point three percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.00,0:04:43.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}just four point three points shy of the fully symmetric architecture,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.55,0:04:47.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and all with only approximate weight symmetry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.09,0:04:50.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Even more importantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.64,0:04:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}this is the first time this family of methods trains at all on ImageNet thirty-two by thirty-two,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.19,0:04:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reaching thirty-one point four percent Top-1 and fifty-five point two percent Top-5.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.73,0:05:01.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Throughout training,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.28,0:05:04.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the homeostatic loss steadily raises the Jacobian's symmetry and tightens the alignment
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.82,0:05:08.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}between EP's error signals and true backprop.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.67,0:05:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The ablations cleanly separate the two biases.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.64,0:05:16.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On Fashion MNIST, when the nudge is made large, classic one-sided EP falls apart,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.61,0:05:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}its error ballooning to thirty-eight point four percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.57,0:05:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The holomorphic Cauchy-integral estimate with six points instead stays at fourteen point three percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.54,0:05:28.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}essentially matching the true derivative at fourteen point seven percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.51,0:05:32.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}proof that finite-nudge bias is fully removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.48,0:05:36.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Separately,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.45,0:05:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}dropping from the exact derivative to a coarse two-point estimate costs about three points on CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.42,0:05:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}quantifying the residual nudge bias.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.38,0:05:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And an architecture whose output feeds straight back to the first layer,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.35,0:05:52.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with no reciprocal connections, benefits just as much,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.32,0:05:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}confirming the loss targets functional symmetry rather than weight symmetry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.59,0:05:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To put the numbers in one place: on CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.52,0:06:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the homeostatic loss lifts asymmetric EP from sixty point four to eighty-four point three percent accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.49,0:06:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}closing the gap to the symmetric network to just four point three points.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.25,0:06:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On ImageNet thirty-two by thirty-two,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.66,0:06:19.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}EP reaches thirty-one point four percent Top-1 and fifty-five point two percent Top-5,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.26,0:06:21.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the first result of its kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.15,0:06:23.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And on Fashion MNIST, using a large nudge,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.88,0:06:31.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the exact holomorphic estimate cuts error from thirty-eight point four percent down to fourteen point three percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.74,0:06:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is that equilibrium propagation does not actually need perfectly symmetric weights.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.70,0:06:41.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}By removing finite-nudge bias exactly with a Cauchy integral,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.49,0:06:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and by encouraging functional symmetry of the Jacobian with a homeostatic loss instead of the weights,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.83,0:06:54.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}asymmetric networks can finally scale to ImageNet-level tasks with only a small gap to the ideal case.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.16,0:06:56.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because functional symmetry is a weaker,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.65,0:06:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}more achievable condition than weight symmetry,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.57,0:07:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}this opens a biologically plausible path to training real physical neural substrates,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.85,0:07:08.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and hints that brains might rely on similar homeostatic mechanisms.
